<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dawro Zone</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dawro Zone is an administrative zone of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, between the Omo and Gojeb rivers, with its centre at Tarcha. It takes its name from the Dawro people and their former kingdom, conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> in 1891, and it contains the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halala-kella">Halala Kella</a>, a long defensive stone wall attributed to the kingdom's rulers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dawro-zone.jpg" alt="Dawro Zone" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Ethiopia adm location map.svg: User:NordNordWest Derivative work: User:SUM1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_zones_of_Ethiopia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
